# AUTHORS -- the copyright holders of REPLACE-PROJECT-TITLE.
#
# This is not the contributor list, and the difference is the whole reason the
# file exists. CONTRIBUTORS.md credits the people who worked on the project.
# This file names who holds copyright in it -- which for anyone contributing
# under a corporate agreement is their employer, not them. The two lists are
# different lengths and neither substitutes for the other.
#
# What it buys you: copyright notices that do not have to be rewritten. Instead
# of naming every holder in every source file and re-editing them all whenever
# the list changes, notices point here:
#
#     Copyright (C) <year> The REPLACE-PROJECT-TITLE Authors
#
# and this file is the list they point at. Change it once, and every notice in
# the project is current. Modern practice pairs that with a one-line SPDX tag
# rather than the full license paragraph:
#
#     // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Adopting this file is therefore a decision about the source tree, not about
# this file alone. It does not change LICENSE and cannot: that file is the
# license itself, reproduced verbatim under its own terms, and the
# angle-bracket fields in its appendix are instructions for what to write in
# your files, not blanks to fill in there.
#
# It is worth having when contributions arrive from more than one legal entity,
# when a contributor agreement is in play, or when files are likely to be
# copied out of this repository on their own. A single-author project gets
# nothing from it that a name in the notice does not already give.
#
# Format is convention, not a specification -- nothing parses this file. One
# entity per line, name then contact, most-significant first. Keep entries that
# no longer contribute: copyright does not lapse when someone stops.

REPLACE-COPYRIGHT-HOLDER
